22:06:03 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Testosterone can influence some behaviors in some contexts—such as reward sensitivity, competitiveness, risk-taking, or aggression—but it does not provide a simple explanation for men being inherently unintelligent, unable to organize, or incapable of care and responsibility. Hormones are only one influence among many. Their effects vary by dose, development, situation, stress, personality, and learned habits. They also do not determine whether someone uses a calendar, notices laundry, remembers a child’s appointment, listens to a partner, or follows through on a commitment. So it is reasonable to say that biology may contribute to average behavioral tendencies in some circumstances. It is not well supported to conclude that testosterone makes a boy destined to be careless or academically unable to keep up. For her son, the useful approach is still concrete: give structure, teach planning and emotional regulation, make responsibility routine, and hold him to clear expectations. If he has persistent attention, impulsivity, or learning difficulties, address those as individual needs with his teacher and a qualified health professional—not as an inevitable consequence of being male.
